item.description:
In the LTK preview, select each changed Java file and inspect
its combined diff. Confirm that:



• only an OK code is removed from a Status constructor;

• the String or Class plug-in identity remains present;

• message and throwable remain unchanged;

• nonzero application-specific codes are not proposed;



Deselect an entire file when its complete proposed change
should not be applied.

After applying the cleanup:



1. compile the affected plug-in projects;

2. run logging and error-handling tests;

3. inspect status consumers that depend on getPlugin() or
   getCode();

4. use Eclipse Undo to restore the complete cleanup operation
   when validation fails.



The cleanup itself is conservative, but normal build and test
validation remains part of a safe refactoring workflow.
